<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<project xmlns="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
		xsi:schemaLocation="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0 http://maven.apache.org/maven-v4_0_0.xsd">
	<modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>
	<parent>
		<groupId>org.openmrs.module</groupId>
		<artifactId>daherendadmission</artifactId>
		<version>1.0.0</version>
	</parent>

	<artifactId>daherendadmission-omod</artifactId>
	<packaging>jar</packaging>
	<name>Daher End Maternity Admission OMOD</name>
	<description>OMOD project for Daher End Maternity Admission</description>

	<dependencies>
		<dependency>
			<groupId>org.openmrs.module</groupId>
			<artifactId>daherendadmission-api</artifactId>
			<version>${project.parent.version}</version>
		</dependency>
		<dependency>
			<groupId>org.openmrs.web</groupId>
			<artifactId>openmrs-web</artifactId>
			<scope>provided</scope>
		</dependency>
		<dependency>
			<groupId>junit</groupId>
			<artifactId>junit</artifactId>
			<version>4.13.2</version>
			<scope>test</scope>
		</dependency>
	</dependencies>

	<build>
		<finalName>${project.parent.artifactId}-${project.parent.version}</finalName>
		<plugins>
			<plugin>
				<groupId>org.openmrs.maven.plugins</groupId>
				<artifactId>maven-openmrs-plugin</artifactId>
			</plugin>
			<plugin>
				<groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
				<artifactId>maven-dependency-plugin</artifactId>
				<!--
				DH-CI-001: the inherited maven-parent-openmrs-module pluginManagement binds this
				plugin's "Expand resources" execution (goal unpack-dependencies, unpacking the
				sibling reactor artifact daherendadmission-api's *.xml/*.properties into this
				module's target/classes) to the generate-resources phase, which runs before
				package. Under a reactor-wide `mvn test` (this repo's CI invocation, and the only
				place these OMOD tests ever actually run; the real packaging build in
				openmrs-config/Dockerfile uses -Dmaven.test.skip=true package), the sibling
				daherendadmission-api module has not been packaged into a JAR yet. Maven only runs
				each reactor module's lifecycle up to the requested phase (test, which comes before
				package), so the artifact this goal needs to unpack from genuinely does not exist
				yet, regardless of which OMOD-local phase this execution is bound to. This is the
				documented MDEP-98 pitfall, reproduced live via `mvn -B test` from the reactor root
				(PARENT and API succeed, OMOD fails at exactly this execution).

				Rebinding to prepare-package, the last standard lifecycle phase before package,
				keeps this a build-configuration-only change with two properties, both live
				verified: (1) under `mvn test`, prepare-package is never reached, since it comes
				after test in the standard lifecycle, so this execution simply does not run and
				cannot fail; both OMOD test classes (CreateTestOrderServletTest,
				DaherExternalConfigurationInterceptorTest) were confirmed to run and pass, proving
				they never needed these unpacked resources in the first place. (2) under a full
				reactor `mvn package`/`install` (the Dockerfile's actual packaging path), Maven
				completes each reactor module's full lifecycle through the requested phase before
				moving to the next dependent module, so daherendadmission-api is already packaged
				by the time this module reaches prepare-package; confirmed via
				`mvn -f pom.xml -Dmaven.test.skip=true package`, which still produces
				omod/target/daherendadmission-1.0.0.omod with the resources correctly unpacked,
				exactly matching the Dockerfile's own invocation.
				-->
				<executions>
					<execution>
						<id>Expand resources</id>
						<phase>prepare-package</phase>
						<goals>
							<goal>unpack-dependencies</goal>
						</goals>
						<configuration>
							<includeGroupIds>org.openmrs.module</includeGroupIds>
							<includeArtifactIds>daherendadmission-api,daherendadmission-omod,daherendadmission-omod-common</includeArtifactIds>
							<includeScope>compile</includeScope>
							<includes>*.xml,*.properties</includes>
							<outputDirectory>${project.build.outputDirectory}</outputDirectory>
						</configuration>
					</execution>
				</executions>
			</plugin>
		</plugins>
	</build>
</project>
